@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Option Desk - A permitted snapshot through local MCP

actor "Agent" as A
participant "Local MCP" as M
participant "chain.run" as C
participant "Snapshot parser" as P
database "Artifact directory" as D
A -> M : option_chain_snapshot\nsource_text or source_data + rights acknowledgement
M -> C : validated tool arguments
C -> P : parse CSV / JSON; normalize fields
alt rights, source, spot or contract fields invalid
 P --> C : validation error
 C --> M : failure
 M --> A : tool error; previous artifact preserved
else permitted, valid input
 P --> C : normalized snapshot with provenance
 C -> C : validate chain_snapshot schema
 C -> D : archive previous file, then atomic write
 C --> M : artifact summary and quality flags
 M --> A : structured result
end
note over A,D
This is a control-flow diagram, not a measured market run.
Imported IV is retained. It is not re-solved from a synthetic quote.
The provider route is separate and subject to provider-access checks.
end note

caption Source: shell/src/optiondesk/cli/chain.py and mcp/server.py. Happy and failure paths use supplied inputs.
@enduml
